    "name": "Fauna of the Stone Age: Chelonioidea",
    "text": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A collection of sea turtles of the super family </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Chelonioidea</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, these reptiles will add life to the temperate, subtropical, and tropical marine ecosystems of your world, acting as ambience, and potential food.</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This mod includes:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span></p>\n<div class=\"spoiler\">\n<div class=\"spoiler-toggle\">Stats</div>\n<div class=\"spoiler-text\">\n<table dir=\"ltr\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px;\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" data-sheets-root=\"1\" data-sheets-baot=\"1\"><colgroup><col width=\"159\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /><col width=\"100\" /></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Common Name</td>\n<td>Scientific name</td>\n<td>Category</td>\n<td>Weight</td>\n<td>Health</td>\n<td>Height</td>\n<td>Damage</td>\n<td>Temp</td>\n<td>Precip</td>\n<td>Foliage Needs</td>\n<td>Altitude</td>\n<td>Group Size</td>\n<td>Meat Drops</td>\n<td>Fat Drops</td>\n<td>Hide Drops</td>\n<td>Other Drops</td>\n<td>Movement</td>\n<td>Diet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Loggerhead sea turtle</td>\n<td>Caretta caretta</td>\n<td>Chelonioidea</td>\n<td>140/0.1</td>\n<td>15/2</td>\n<td>2.1L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>10-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>9-10</td>\n<td>2+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Green sea turtle</td>\n<td>Chelonia mydas</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>135/0.1</td>\n<td>14/2</td>\n<td>1.5L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>6-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>9-10</td>\n<td>2+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>vegetables, grass</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Leatherback sea turtle</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>Dermochelys coriacea</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>475/0.1</td>\n<td>48/2</td>\n<td>2.7L</td>\n<td>3t1</td>\n<td>8-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>15-17</td>\n<td>4-5</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hawksbill sea turtle</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>Eretmochelys imbricata</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>80/0.1</td>\n<td>8/2</td>\n<td>1L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>12-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>4-5</td>\n<td>1+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Atlantic ridley sea turtle</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>Lepidochelys kempii</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>40/0.1</td>\n<td>5/2</td>\n<td>0.5L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>4-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>2-3</td>\n<td>1+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Pacific ridley sea turtle</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>Lepidochelys olivacea</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>45/0.1</td>\n<td>6/2</td>\n<td>0.6L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>10-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>2-3</td>\n<td>1+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flatback sea turtle</td>\n<td>\n<div>\n<div>Natator depressus</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>80/0.1</td>\n<td>8/2</td>\n<td>1.2L</td>\n<td>2t1</td>\n<td>12-40</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>All</td>\n<td>0-1.0</td>\n<td>1,1-5</td>\n<td>4-5</td>\n<td>1+-0.3</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Shell</td>\n<td>Swimming</td>\n<td>fish, vegetables</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Features:</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">All species have a unique shell that can be used to craft bone meal, and a taxidermied full body.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">And a big thanks to everyone who gave feedback and assistance!</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /><br /></span></p>\n<div class=\"spoiler\">\n<div class=\"spoiler-toggle\">FAQ</div>\n<div class=\"spoiler-text\"><strong>Q:</strong> Why so many animal packs? Can't you make one giant one?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> The combined size of this series exceeds the Mod data base's file upload size limit and therefore could not be hosted on this site, making it extremely difficult for servers to use. What's more, I don't know just how large certain clade file sizes will get as new features come out and I want to ensure they don't need to be split in the future, as that may cause considerable server issues. Whenever mod packs are implemented, or if there are other resources for creating a more organized bundle, I will do so.<br /><br /><br /><br /><strong>Q:</strong> Is this mod safe to add and remove to an existing world?<br /><br /><strong>A:</strong> Yes, this mod series is safe to add and remove. Items from this mod that have been placed will be invisible or appear as question blocks if the mod is removed but can be safely broken.</div>\n</div>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br /><br />All Rights Reserved. Please contact me if you are interested in making work derived from mine.<br /></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
